symptoms. No two people with that are exactly the same in terms of the timing of the symptoms. But I would say October tends to be a window where the first early onset symptoms, start occurring, and then they pick up momentum in November with a lot more symptoms in December. And January and February tend to be the worst months. Those are the months where the largest proportion of people are going to be in a full-blown major repressive episode among those who have the seasonal pattern to their depression. Do you think that's tied into just the end of the year, all the things going on that might

