keep someone busy, maybe distracted the holidays, that sort of thing? Does that have anything to do with why it might be worse? now it's January and February? I think that it does. There's not a lot of research on this, but I do find that a lot of people kind of make it through the holidays with a lot of effort because they're typically dealing with a lot of fatigue at that time. But there's so many activities that we have to be present for during the holidays, pressure to be at social activities, work holiday parties, those kinds of things. So from a behavioral perspective, those help to keep us a bit more engaged during

